0628067436,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":98.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.01128,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":7.5,"_gate_insider_buying":1.0,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Millrose Properties, Inc. is the premier permanent capital solution for residential homebuilders and developers. The company specializes in the acquisition, financing and development of residential land through long-term, capital-efficient structures. The company also provides homebuilders with a predictable, just-in-time supply of finished homesites \u0096 the scarcest and mission-critical resource in the homebuilding industry. Millrose utilizes a proprietary technology platform that provides real-time feedback and data analytics to drive acquisition decisions. Every transaction in the Millrose portfolio undergoes rigorous independent due diligence to ensure attractive yields and long-term viability. By enabling an asset-light model, Millrose provides its diverse roster of homebuilder partners with the strategic flexibility to maintain production volumes and optimize balance sheet efficiency across all market environments. Millrose Properties, Inc.is based in Miami, United States.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Darren  Lewis Richman | CEO & President | Age 53","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Millrose Properties, Inc. is a mid-cap real estate business with a $4.3B market cap on $600M of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","Accruals are elevated at -35.6% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 5.3\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 6.9% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 4.1\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 102% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"News sentiment running negative (-0.12) across recent coverage","sev":"amber","cat":"news"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 58% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 17% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Millrose Properties (NYSE:MRP) versus Farmland Partners (NYSE:FPI) Head-To-He